# Nothing under private/ is a web address on a server.
#
# This tree was the OD9 tenant's LOCAL admin scaffolding: wrapper pages that
# required the shared platform by a Windows path (C:/xampp/...), a bootstrap that
# did the same, mail partials, migrations and a log. On the server none of the
# pages could run, and until 2026-11-22 every one of them could still be REQUESTED.
# That night a scanner asked for 70 of them in two seconds: 68 answered with a PHP
# fault (which paged as four new fault shapes), and one, generate-wrappers.php
# (deleted the same day), checked no login and wrote 36 files into this tree. It
# had done the same on 2026-09-24. Cloudflare refuses /private/ from most places;
# the origin did not, and private/logs/security.log was served to anyone it let
# through.
#
# Later the same day the wrapper pages, their router and the bootstrap were retired
# from the repository and from the server (the admin is the shared platform's). The
# mail partials and migrations stay in the repository and are no longer deployed, so
# on a server this file is the only thing in the folder. It stays on purpose: a file
# that comes back here (a rollback restores removed files) is still not served, and
# the fleet sweep asks the server for a name in this folder every day and expects 403.
#
# The test is the DOCUMENT ROOT, which the server sets and a visitor cannot: a
# docroot that starts with a drive letter is the local XAMPP checkout, one
# developer's machine, and is left open. Anything else is a server, and is refused.
#   https://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/expr.html (read 2026-11-22: DOCUMENT_ROOT, !~)
#   https://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/sections.html (read 2026-11-22: <If> merges last)
# That page does not say an authorization rule works inside <If>, so it is PROVEN,
# not assumed: tests/check_origin_refusals.py plants the same rule with the test
# reversed in a scratch folder on local Apache and requires a 403 from it.
<If "%{DOCUMENT_ROOT} !~ /^[A-Za-z]:/">
    Require all denied
</If>
